      "title": "How much storage?",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "Photos are the big one: 1M uploads × 2 MB = **2 TB per day**. Over a year that’s ~730 TB.\n\nData is usually stored three times so a dead disk loses nothing — so plan for about **2 PB** in year one. That rules out “one database server” immediately.",
