      "short": "Bandwidth",
      "title": "How much network?",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "Uploads are the small part: 2 TB a day is about 20 MB/s coming in. Viewing is the big part: if each user looks at 100 photos a day as 200 KB thumbnails, that’s **200 TB a day** going out.\n\n200 TB ÷ 100,000 s ≈ 2 GB/s — about 16 Gbit/s on average, more at peak. That’s a job for a CDN, not ten web servers.",
